.TH CB_INSERT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cb_insert \- Insert a key-value pair into a Critbit tree

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cb_internal.h>

.IB int
.IB cb_insert (
.IB critbit_tree* cb,
.IB const void* key,
.IB size_t keylen
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcb_insert\fR function inserts a key-value pair into a Critbit tree. The key is a pointer to a buffer containing the key data, and \fBkeylen\fR specifies the length of the key.

The function takes three arguments:
.TP
.IR cb (critbit_tree*)
A pointer to the Critbit tree where the key-value pair will be inserted.
.TP
.IR key (const void*)
A pointer to the buffer containing the key data.
.TP
.IR keylen (size_t)
The length of the key.

The function returns one of the following values:
.TP
.B CB_SUCCESS
The key-value pair was successfully inserted into the tree.
.TP
.B CB_EXISTS
The key already exists in the tree, and the insertion was not performed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcb_insert\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cb_internal.h>

int main() {
    critbit_tree cb;
    cb_init(&cb);

    const char* key = "example_key";
    size_t keylen = 13;

    int result = cb_insert(&cb, key, keylen);

    if (result == CB_SUCCESS) {
        printf("Key inserted successfully\n");
    } else if (result == CB_EXISTS) {
        printf("Key already exists\n");
    }

    cb_free(&cb);

    return 0;
}
.nef